 "observations": [
  "col_left L3, L4: the z of «azimuth» and the first z of «syzygiae» are printed broken, the middle of their diagonals missing (like ‹⁄›), with a piece of the diagonal standing apart low on the line; read z.",
  "col_left L5, L6, L10, L44, L46, col_right L11, L19, L21, L25, L27: «configurationes», «figurae» (twice, also col_right L10), «difficilius», «fixae» and «fixarum» are printed with the fi and ffi ligatures.",
  "col_left L13, L24: the hyphens of «al-Battānī» (1.7 by 1.1 points, like a point at mid height) and of «al-a‘zal» (2.0 points long) are printed short; read as hyphens. «al-Battānī» has the bars over the second a and the last i.",
  "col_left L14: «8°» is printed with the degree sign.",
  "col_left L16: a short spur hangs under the o of «Sosigenes» (1.8 points wide at the baseline, tapering to 1.0 point below it); it is not a dot below; read o.",
  "col_left L23: «*as-sunbulah*» is printed in italics; «α» is Greek; «as-simāk» has the bar over the a.",
  "col_left L24: «al-a‘zal» has the sign of ‘ayn.",
  "col_left L27: the line is set tight: its word spaces are 1.8–3.1 points (after «Sprenger» 2.3, after «A.» 2.0, before «(em.» 1.8, after «(em.» 2.3, after «n.» 3.1, after «345,» 1.9), against 4–7 points in the other lines; transcribed with spaces. The A of «A.» is printed without its crossbar, like Λ; read A.",
  "col_left L41: «{sc:xxiv}-{sc:v}» is printed so, the second numeral shortened to its last letter. A speck (0.6 by 0.6 point) on the baseline between «{sc:xii}» and «n.» is not transcribed; the point after this n is printed small (1.0 by 1.2 points).",
  "col_left L46: «quantae a Ptolemaeo» is printed with broken letters (the t without its crossbar, the o of «Ptolemaeo» open, the last e like c); read quantae a Ptolemaeo.",
  "col_right L2, L23: «tānī» has the bars over the a and the i (2.4 by 1.2 points over the i).",
  "col_right L6: a speck (0.7 by 0.8 point) at the foot of the t of «et», 1.3–2.1 points above the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L4, L25, L28, L41: the hyphens of «vi-» (1.8 points long), «*144-*» (2.2), «semi-» (2.2) and «ar-Raḥmān» (1.9) are printed short; read as hyphens.",
  "col_right L14: the ball of the second 2 of «292-293» is printed apart from the figure by a hairline gap, like a point over it; read 292.",
  "col_right L16: a round speck (1.2 by 1.3 points), 0.4–1.7 points above the baseline, between the c and the h of «Hipparchum» is not transcribed: it is smaller than the points of this type (1.5–2.0 points across) and stands above the baseline.",
  "col_right L21: the M of «Menelao» is printed blotted over its left half, with a stroke (1.4 points) rising above its top, read at 4,000 dpi; read M.",
  "col_right L31: the 9 of «196» is printed smeared; read 196. The lower left foot of the third X of «{sc:xxxv}» stands apart like a point; it is not a point.",
  "col_right L33, L34: «Stiffe» is printed with the ff ligature and its e broken; «Stöffler» with the diaeresis on the o and the ffl ligature; the h of «Joh.» is printed broken, like li; read Joh.",
  "col_right L35: the o of «Strabo» is printed broken, its right side apart; read o.",
  "col_right L38, L46: the comma of the semicolon after «211 n.» and the comma after «175)» are printed short (1.9 by 2.5 and 1.8 by 2.4 points, their feet 0.7–0.9 point below the baseline).",
  "col_right L39: «*Ṣubbī*» and «*Ṣubbah*» are printed in italics, with the dots under the S and the bar over the i.",
  "col_right L41: «aṣ-Ṣūfī» has the dots under the s and the S and the bars over the u and the i; the arm of the f runs into the bar over the i (together 5.5 points long), read at 8,000 dpi; «‘Abd» begins with the sign of ‘ayn; «ar-Raḥmān» has the dot under the h and the bar over the second a.",
